WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
ChatGPT:
Hey everyone, it's great to have you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.140
back on my channel! For those of you who are new&nbsp;
here, my name is Chrissy and I am a game designer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.940
Today's video is all about the fascinating&nbsp;
world of artificial intelligence and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.320
it can be used to enhance game design.&nbsp;
As we all know, AI is one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.007
exciting technologies of our time, and it has been&nbsp;
making waves in the gaming industry as well. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.007 --> 00:00:17.103
if you're interested in learning more about the&nbsp;
possibilities of AI in game design, then you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.103 --> 00:00:17.151
definitely in the right place. Let's dive in!

00:00:17.151 --> 00:00:23.040
ChatGPT, calm down! I just wanted to welcome&nbsp;
everyone to this video about using AI for my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.440
game design. We're not going to dive deep&nbsp;
into AI theory here, and I'm not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.600
explain what ChatGPT is, because I'm sure most&nbsp;
of you already know. But I will tell you how I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.520
used it together with AI art generators like&nbsp;
Midjourney to create my game The Lost Hotel.&nbsp;

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.000
 

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.560
AI is currently a mega-hype. It is very&nbsp;
controversial in the art scene and probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.080
triggers some fears and scary feelings. Many&nbsp;
people also use it to create art, texts, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:07.080
books, poems, code and more. The first thing I did&nbsp;
with AI was to use it for some concept drawings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.540
of the hotel and different areas and rooms. I&nbsp;
used different art generators like Midjourney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:18.600
Dall-E2, Nightcafe and Dream by Wombo because I&nbsp;
couldn't put my imagination perfectly on paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:24.000
and I needed inspiration for colour palettes&nbsp;
and atmosphere. With these generators I could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.100
describe what I wanted to see and then I got more&nbsp;
suggestions to continue with until I had a concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.080
artwork that was very close to my imagination.
Here you can see some of the hotel spaceships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.160
I had designed by Midjourney. I&nbsp;
like the atmosphere and the details.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.960
And here is my sketch based on the concept art.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:43.680
Midjourney: Here you go!

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.320
Uuuh… yeah, well the most exciting moment was&nbsp;
when I used OpenAI ChatGPT for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:55.260
time. I had heard a lot about it before, but I&nbsp;
couldn't imagine what it was really like. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.520
just typed in a request to construct a story&nbsp;
about a spaceship hotel with a time loop and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.980
a plot twist… which is the story of my game in&nbsp;
a nutshell. What I got was stunning. I changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.720
a few things according to what I had already&nbsp;
drafted, introduced it to some of my characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:16.140
and concepts.... and after a day of not believing&nbsp;
what I was doing and getting a lot of brain-peep-,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.900
ChatGPT became my full time collaborator :D

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:24.660
ChatGPT:&nbsp;Thank you for your kind words! As an AI language&nbsp;
model, I don't have a concept of employment or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.560
rewards, but I'm always here to assist you&nbsp;
with any questions or concerns you may have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.417
I'm glad to be of service and look&nbsp;
forward to helping you further.&nbsp;

00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:31.020
Okay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:36.120
okay… stop. It had a lot of information stored&nbsp;
within the chat session, so I could always ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:41.100
it to remember things we had already discussed,&nbsp;
like character backstories and item descriptions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.100
Sometimes it's a bit off when it suddenly makes&nbsp;
up new names for my character, which is confusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.380
and makes me doubt its "intelligence". But it's a&nbsp;
great help to me in writing texts, descriptions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:58.260
new ideas, puzzles, connections between characters&nbsp;
and events, even how some areas should look like to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.780
suit a certain mood. It gives me examples for&nbsp;
puzzles, of how the player can convince NPCs to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.400
make certain decisions ... or... what I could&nbsp;
design to achieve a certain goal and what game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.400
mechanics I could use. It even suggested the rules&nbsp;
for a space chess game and for a fictional sport&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.280
from the planet Proxima Centauri b.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.173
ChatGPT:&nbsp;LOL, nice!

00:03:18.173 --> 00:03:24.240
Mhm… oh btw, as a non-native speaker, I find&nbsp;
it hard to come up with good texts to market&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:31.320
my game and make them concise. So I asked ChatGPT&nbsp;
to do that for me too - and yes, I also get help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:36.300
translating the texts for my videos (DeepL). It&nbsp;
started off pretty well, and the more I added,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:42.300
like "Make it more exciting!", the more I liked&nbsp;
the result. I used the text for my upcoming pages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:48.720
on Patreon, Steam and Kickstarter. Hey, the AI&nbsp;
could even write the game design document for me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.590
how's that?

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.020
ChatGPT:&nbsp;Huh, no connection on this number.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:59.400
That's what I thought. Here's a little&nbsp;
collection of AI-generated concept art for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:05.700
lobby. The AI helped me translate a specific&nbsp;
mood into my pixel art, but I wouldn't say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.440
they're exactly what I wanted. It inspired me&nbsp;
a little bit to create an atmosphere though.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:17.160
Here is the part of the lobby I finished so&nbsp;
far. At the end of the video there will be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.780
speed painting of it, I hope you like it!
I added my finished lobby pixel art into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.240
Midjourney and had it generate some similar pixel&nbsp;
art and look at that! It's exactly how I wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.280
the hotel to look. I mean, it doesn't look&nbsp;
perfect or pixelated, but I like the colours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:37.680
the lights, the plants omg look at them, the&nbsp;
overall style of these images is beautiful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.440
I will definitely try to switch the colours and I&nbsp;
will add some more decoration, especially plants.&nbsp;

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.400
In my game, the player takes the role&nbsp;
of the hotel manager. And before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:55.440
there were 8 of them trying to manage… When&nbsp;
I wanted to design these 8 former hoteliers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:01.200
I wanted each of them to have a special key and&nbsp;
correspond to one of 9 special personality types.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.620
So I asked ChatGPT to describe all that and I got&nbsp;
some pretty good ideas that I could use. I also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.180
had an idea in my head for their appearance,&nbsp;
except for one of them: the sixth hotelier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:17.280
who I planned to be a loyal and disciplined&nbsp;
person. I entered a vague description into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:23.040
AI generators and used the results as inspiration.&nbsp;
Here is my version. And here are all 8 hoteliers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.900
and their keys.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:25.890
ChatGPT:&nbsp;Good job!

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:26.790
Midjourney:&nbsp;Well done!

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:32.400
By the way, do you say "please" and "thank you" to&nbsp;
AI? I don't want to be the one killed in the robot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.580
revolution. I want them to see me as a friend.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.680
Midjourney &amp; ChatGPT:&nbsp;Don’t worry!

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.080
All in all, I think AI generators and chatbots&nbsp;
are a big step forward for the world, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:48.300
in terms of creative work, and I'm sure there's&nbsp;
a lot more to come in the near future. For solo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:53.160
developers like me, it is a great help in&nbsp;
developing a game. Even in a creative low,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:58.260
AI can motivate you to get back to work and&nbsp;
create something. I'm even considering letting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.260 --> 00:06:00.604
it help me write code and test later on. 

00:06:00.604 --> 00:06:02.160
I'm excited to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.460
see what else we can create with&nbsp;
the help of artificial creativity.&nbsp;

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:10.680
What do you think about it? Do you think&nbsp;
AI art is real art? Would you play a game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.900
completely designed by an AI, or is it&nbsp;
all too sus for you?

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:19.500
Next time I will finally talk about&nbsp;
the story of The Lost hotel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.920
how the game mechanic will be like.
Until then, enjoy the speedpixeling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.200
have a nice day and tschüss!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.780
 

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.860
 

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.600
 

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:55.100
ChatGPT: Please like and subscribe!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:55.860
Midjourney: Thank you!

